{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — product badge filter.

  Aloha, 3 September 2026: "Please remove every Limited Edition label or badge
  from the product cards, product recommendations and any other part of the
  website. […] We do not want to turn that reality into scarcity language that
  pressures customers into buying quickly."

  Luxe draws card and product badges from two store-side sources:
    · product tags prefixed `Badge:`      e.g. "Badge: Limited Edition"
    · the `custom.badges` metafield       a list of strings

  Both are product DATA, not theme code, so deleting the theme markup would not
  remove the words — and re-adding one tag in the admin would put them straight
  back. This snippet is the gate instead: every place Luxe prints a badge now
  prints them through here, and any label on the suppression list is dropped
  before it reaches the page. A tag left behind in the admin is harmless.

  The list is a theme setting (Hartwick — Material Archive > Badges), so Aloha
  can add a phrase without a developer. Matching is case-insensitive and matches
  on containment, so "Limited Edition", "LIMITED EDITION" and "Limited Edition —
  25 pieces" are all suppressed by the single entry "limited edition".

  This suppresses promotional scarcity language only. A verified production
  quantity still belongs on the page — as a factual row in the Material Record
  ("Production quantity: 25 pieces"), never as a badge.

  Usage — capture, so the caller can tell whether anything survived the filter
  and skip the wrapper element entirely when nothing did:

    {%- capture ha_badges -%}{%- render 'ha-badges', product: card_product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if ha_badges != blank -%}<div class="…">{{ ha_badges }}</div>{%- endif -%}

  `class:` puts a class on each span, for the one caller (featured-product) whose
  badges are not inside a wrapper of their own.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign suppressed = settings.ha_suppressed_badges | default: 'limited edition, limited-edition, limited run, exclusive, last chance, selling fast, almost gone, only a few left, hurry, final pieces' | downcase | split: ','

  assign labels = ''

  for tag in product.tags
    if tag contains 'Badge:'
      assign label = tag | remove_first: 'Badge:' | strip
      assign labels = labels | append: '|@|' | append: label
    endif
  endfor

  for badge in product.metafields.custom.badges.value
    assign label = badge | strip
    assign labels = labels | append: '|@|' | append: label
  endfor

  assign labels = labels | remove_first: '|@|' | split: '|@|'
-%}

{%- for label in labels -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign haystack = label | downcase
    assign blocked = false
    for phrase in suppressed
      assign needle = phrase | strip
      if needle != blank and haystack contains needle
        assign blocked = true
        break
      endif
    endfor
  -%}
  {%- unless blocked -%}<span{% if class != blank %} class="{{ class }}"{% endif %}>{{ label }}</span>{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}
